Actually there is an regression on this test:

```
extension<S, T : IArray<S>> T : IFoo<S>
{ 
    S getFirst()
    {
        return this[0];
    }
}
```

This extension should also be allowed, because although the target type `T` does not directly reference `S`, there is a constraint on `T` that references `S`. 

So we need to extend the logic to be: if a generic parameter on an extension is not used by target type or by any other `supType` in `GenericTypeConstraintDecl` of the parent `GenericDecl`, then it is an error.

