This PR adds a new `addComponents(routes)` function to the global apprun instance that allows registering multiple component-route pairs in a single call, providing a convenient way to set up multiple components at once.

## Problem

Currently, developers need to manually mount components and register routes individually:

```typescript
// Current approach - verbose and repetitive
const homeComponent = new HomeComponent();
homeComponent.mount('#home-container');

const aboutComponent = new AboutComponent();  
aboutComponent.mount('#about-container');

app.start('#counter-container', counterModel, counterView, counterUpdate);
```

## Solution

The new `addComponents` function provides a declarative way to register multiple components:

```typescript
// Use addComponents to register all route-component pairs
app.addComponents('#pages', {
  '/': HomeComponent,
  '/about': AboutComponent,
  '/contact': ContactComponent,
  '/counter': CounterComponent
});
```

